  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 5.2,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.96,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings level off at about 1.05–1.12 from 9 h to 18 h. That flat line could be a real stationary phase, or it could be the reader hitting its upper limit. Dilution tests show it is the reader's limit. The 18 h aliquot diluted 10x read 0.5245 and 0.5157 (mean 0.520), which works out to about 5.20. Diluted 20x it read 0.2575 and 0.267 (mean 0.262), which works out to about 5.24. The two dilutions agree within about 1%, so diluted samples give readings in proportion to biomass. On that basis the true 18 h OD is about 5.2, roughly 4.7 times the undiluted 1.10. The 12 h aliquot diluted 10x read 0.522, about 5.2 corrected, so the true level was already about 5.2 at 12 h and the undiluted readings were capped then too. As a check of the low range, the 6 h aliquot diluted 10x read 0.0237, about 0.24 corrected, versus 0.279 undiluted. That is roughly in line given how weak the diluted signal is, and it was not saturated. So the plateau near 1.1 is caused by the reader saturating, not by growth stopping: biomass over the final hours is well above what the undiluted readings show, at about OD 5.2. One limit: only the 12 h and 18 h aliquots were tested in the late period. Both gave the same corrected value of about 5.2, but the 13–17 h aliquots were not checked directly."
  },
